# Cline Rules for SeeThrough Project

## TypeORM Entity Relations

Every TypeORM entity relation field decorated with @ManyToOne, @OneToMany, @OneToOne, or @ManyToMany MUST use the `Relation<T>` wrapper type from `typeorm` instead of just `T`, where `T` is the relation entity type.

```typescript
// CORRECT
import { type Relation } from 'typeorm';

@ManyToOne(() => User, (user) => user.sessions, { onDelete: 'CASCADE' })
user: Relation<User>;

@OneToMany(() => Session, (session) => session.user)
sessions: Relation<Session[]>;
```

```typescript
// WRONG - do NOT do this
@ManyToOne(() => User, (user) => user.sessions, { onDelete: 'CASCADE' })
user: User;

@OneToMany(() => Session, (session) => session.user)
sessions: Session[];
```

This ensures proper type safety when working with TypeORM's lazy/loaded relations.